// M4: spawn ONE isolate over a MOVED bundle inside a `scope`, observe its effect. The bundle carries a
// raw pointer to a slot main owns plus the value to write; the worker writes through it on its own thread.
// The `scope` joins the child at its closing brace, and that join happens-before main's read — so there is
// no data race (this fixture is the KAMA_TSAN shared-nothing proof) while still proving the worker ran.
//
// ⚠️ COPY THE MOVE, NOT THE POINTER. What this fixture is ABOUT is the moved bundle: ownership crosses to
// the isolate, so the parent provably cannot touch it afterwards. The `UnsafePtr` is how a fixture written
// before M4.2 observed the effect, and it is a legal crossing (SPEC, *the three sharing seams*: a raw
// pointer crosses, the join is what orders the write against the parent's read). But it is NOT how you
// should write "let a child write into something I keep" today — `tests/parfor_in_scope.kama` does exactly
// that with `spawn bump(x: ref side)`, no `unsafe` and no pointer, because the borrow mode the scope
// licenses did not exist when this was written. Reach for a moved bundle when the isolate should OWN its
// state; reach for `ref` when the parent keeps it.
import { std::concurrent::Isolate };

type resource Payload {
    UnsafePtr<int32> dst;
    int32 value;

    public unsafe ctor make(ref int32 dst, int32 value) {
        this.dst = addr(of: dst);
        this.value = value;
    }

    // Write the value through the slot — runs on the isolate's own thread.
    public unsafe fn void run() {
        this.dst[0] = this.value;
    }
}

fn void worker(Payload p) {   // owns the bundle by value (the caller `give`s it in)
    p.run();
}

fn int32 main() {
    int32 result = 0;
    Payload p = Payload.make(dst: ref result, value: 42i32);
    scope {
        spawn worker(p: give p);   // deferred-join child on a fresh OS thread with the moved bundle
    }                              // BARRIER: the child is joined here, before `result` is read
    return result;               // 42 iff the isolate ran
}
